stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Source
    Source --> Retained: logical deletion / scheduled retention
    Retained --> Source: authorized recovery before irreversible purge
    Source --> DeadHistory: permitted ordinary physical destruction
    Retained --> DeadHistory: retention deadlines reached and purge permitted
    Source --> Source: protected Email / legal hold / enforcement refuses destruction
    Retained --> Retained: recoverable window / hold / enforcement refuses destruction
    DeadHistory --> [*]: authorized legal / retention deletion
    note right of DeadHistory
        APP / COM / ORG remain independent.
        Owner lock, fresh Source lock, fingerprint INSERT,
        and Source DELETE share the owning DB transaction.
        A later destroy failure rolls back the INSERT.
        No transition restores Source from History.
        Due ORG whole-Identity erasure removes its History
        in the same local transaction as Operator deletion.
        APP / COM model erasure checks fresh retention and holds
        before children, then removes only its own histories.
        Source children, History removal and parent DELETE share
        the local transaction; external cleanup is retryable.
        Routine APP / COM retention keeps Identity tombstones.
    end note
